Subject: [PATCH] accept a GART root that carries its PDE flag bits

valid_gart_config() rejects any PAGE_TABLE_BASE_ADDR that is not 4 KiB
aligned. No real root ever is. amdgpu_gmc_pd_addr() ORs the page directory's
flag bits into the low bits of the value it programs, so the register arrives
holding something like 0x6900005 -- 0x6900000 with AMDGPU_PTE_VALID and one
more flag set.

Gfx12GartTranslator::translate() already knows this: it masks the base with
gfx12_pte_address_mask() and uses only the address bits. The precondition,
added by aac939813f, checks the unmasked register instead, so it refuses the
one input the translator was written to accept.

The consequence is not local. publish_gart() returns false, so
MemoryHubBlockModel leaves the VMID-0 bit clear in the GFXHUB invalidation
acknowledge; the guest spins on GCVM_INVALIDATE_ENG17_ACK and dies with
"Timeout waiting for VM flush ACK!". The GART address space is left with no
translator, so every subsequent read through it returns
VmAccessOutcome::Unavailable -- which is why the MES doorbell handler retries
the queue read pointer forever against a single address.

Validate the masked address, which is what is actually dereferenced, and
likewise bound the page table's extent from the masked base.

Measured on gfx1250_mi455x: root=0x6900005 aperture=[0x6c00000000,
0x6c1fffffff], 131072 pages; base_unaligned was the only failing clause.

diff --git a/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp b/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp
index e2b49d68ea..25bdf1936c 100644
--- a/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp
+++ b/emulation/rocjitsu/lib/rocjitsu/src/rocjitsu/vm/amdgpu/gpu_vm.cpp
@@ -62,10 +62,22 @@ constexpr uint64_t gfx12_pde_address_mask(Gfx12VmConfig config) {
 bool valid_gart_config(const GartConfig &config, Gfx12VmConfig vm_config) {
   const uint64_t physical_mask = gfx12_physical_address_mask(vm_config);
   const uint64_t virtual_mask = gfx12_virtual_address_mask(vm_config);
-  if (config.page_table_base == 0 || (config.page_table_base & (kGfx12PageBytes - 1)) != 0 ||
-      (config.page_table_base & physical_mask) != config.page_table_base) {
+  // PAGE_TABLE_BASE_ADDR is not a bare address. The driver ORs the page
+  // directory's flag bits into the low bits before writing it -- amdgpu's
+  // amdgpu_gmc_pd_addr() sets AMDGPU_PTE_VALID and friends -- so a perfectly
+  // legal root arrives here as, say, 0x6900005. Validate what the translator
+  // will actually use: Gfx12GartTranslator::translate() masks the base with
+  // gfx12_pte_address_mask() and ignores those low bits. Requiring the raw
+  // register to be page-aligned rejects every real GART root, leaves the
+  // GFXHUB acknowledge bit clear, and hangs the guest in "Timeout waiting for
+  // VM flush ACK!".
+  //
+  // Only the low flag bits may differ: stripping them must leave exactly the
+  // address the translator will use, so a root that overruns the physical
+  // address width is still refused rather than silently truncated.
+  const uint64_t table = config.page_table_base & gfx12_pte_address_mask(vm_config);
+  if (table == 0 || (config.page_table_base & ~uint64_t{kGfx12PageBytes - 1}) != table)
     return false;
-  }
   if (config.aperture_start > config.aperture_end ||
       (config.aperture_start & (kGfx12PageBytes - 1)) != 0 ||
       (config.aperture_end & (kGfx12PageBytes - 1)) != kGfx12PageBytes - 1 ||
@@ -75,7 +83,7 @@ bool valid_gart_config(const GartConfig &config, Gfx12VmConfig vm_config) {
 
   const uint64_t page_count = (config.aperture_end - config.aperture_start) / kGfx12PageBytes + 1;
   const uint64_t last_pte_offset = (page_count - 1) * sizeof(uint64_t);
-  return last_pte_offset <= physical_mask - config.page_table_base;
+  return last_pte_offset <= physical_mask - table;
 }
 
 Mtype gfx12_mtype(uint64_t entry) {
